        "original_id": "d50bcaa6-9d8e-5191-a03a-4e1306472106",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Glenn Hughes, Dave Evans, Bon Scott, Colin Burgess, George Young, Malcolm Young, Angus Young\n- Bands: Trapeze, Deep Purple, Black Sabbath, AC/DC, Masters Apprentices, The Easybeats\n- Products: From Now On..., Can I Sit Next to You, Girl\n- Roles: bassist, vocalist, singer, drummer, co-producer\n\nFacts:\n- Glenn Hughes was born on 21 August 1951 and is an English rock bassist and vocalist.\n- Dave Evans was born on 20 July 1953 and is an Australian singer.\n- Dave Evans briefly sang for AC/DC from 1973 to 1974.\n- Glenn Hughes is best known for playing bass and performing vocals for Trapeze and for the Mk. lineup of Deep Purple.\n- From Now On... is a solo studio album by former Deep Purple, Black Sabbath, and Trapeze bassist and vocalist Glenn Hughes.\n- A version of Can I Sit Next to You, Girl features lead vocals by Dave Evans before he was replaced by Bon Scott.\n- The version of Can I Sit Next to You, Girl also features drums by former Masters Apprentices member Colin Burgess.\n- The version of Can I Sit Next to You, Girl also features bass guitar by former The Easybeats member George Young, who was the older brother of AC/DC cofounders Malcolm Young and Angus Young and also served as a co-producer.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
